      "updated_at": "2026-10-04T14:31:56Z",
      "body": "**Measured speed-up after merge.** I ran the ~96M chat fine-tune with the same settings on both builds: `dialogue-train`, pointer=32, batch 16, context 384, `mixed-c` corpus, one RTX 4090, with the other GPU busy in both cases.\n\n| Build | Seconds to step 2,000 |\n|---|---|\n| `74d8189` (CPU pointer path) | 924 |\n| main `e8226b76` (CUDA pointer kernels) | 516 |\n\nThat is **1.79× faster**. The run is `chat-100m-Cx`, compared against the morning's `chat-100m-C`. References #820",
